---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@components/ui/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '@components/ui/Section.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '@config/site';
import { withBase } from '@utils/url';

// Phase 9: replaces the Phase 1 "Coming Soon" placeholder with the real
// privacy policy. Content is scoped to only what is verified by
// docs/PRODUCT_CONTEXT.md, docs/ENGINEERING_STANDARDS.md, and the current
// codebase (no analytics/cookies/backend/accounts exist; no microphone or
// third-party SDK usage is documented for the Android app). See this
// phase's report for the full list of facts used and facts intentionally
// omitted because they could not be verified.
const lastUpdated = 'August 2, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How the ${siteConfig.name} website and Android app handle information, in plain English.`}
>
  <PageHero
    title="Privacy Policy"
    subtitle={`How the ${siteConfig.name} website and Android app handle information.`}
  />
  <Section>
    <div class="legal-content">
      <p class="legal-content__updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        {siteConfig.name} is an independent educational product built by {siteConfig.company} to
        help people prepare for the USCIS Civics Test and the citizenship interview. {
          siteConfig.name
        } is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by USCIS or any U.S. government agency.
        This policy explains what information the {siteConfig.name} website and the {
          siteConfig.name
        } Android app use, and how that information is handled.
      </p>

      <h2>Information Collected Through This Website</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not require an account, and it does not use cookies, analytics, or
        advertising tools. Browsing this website does not send your personal information to {
          siteConfig.company
        }. See "Contact Us" below for how information you choose to share with us is used.
      </p>

      <h2>Information the Android App Uses</h2>
      <p>
        The {siteConfig.name} Android app does not require you to create an account. It is
        designed to work as a self-contained study tool for the USCIS Civics Test and the
        citizenship interview, covering civics questions, flashcards, mock tests, and progress
        tools.
      </p>

      <h2>Information Stored on Your Device</h2>
      <p>
        To support your study progress, the app stores certain information locally on your
        device, including:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your favorites</li>
        <li>Your overall progress</li>
        <li>Questions you've marked as weak or answered incorrectly</li>
        <li>Your review schedule, used for spaced review</li>
        <li>Saved local or state-specific answers</li>
        <li>Your mock-test history</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This information stays on your device so the app can pick up where you left off each time
        you return to it.
      </p>

      <h2>Microphone and Speech Recognition</h2>
      <p>
        The app does not currently use your device's microphone or speech recognition. If a
        future version adds a feature that uses the microphone, this policy will be updated
        before that feature is released, and the app will only access the microphone with your
        permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not integrate third-party analytics, advertising, or tracking tools.
        Google Play, described below, is the platform through which the Android app is
        distributed.
      </p>

      <h2>Google Play</h2>
      <p>
        The {siteConfig.name} Android app is distributed through Google Play. When you view the
        app's listing or install {siteConfig.name}, Google Play's own privacy policy and terms
        apply to that process. We encourage you to review Google's privacy policy to understand
        how Google handles information related to your Google Play account and app installs.
      </p>

      <h2>External Links</h2>
      <p>
        This website may link to outside resources, such as official information on USCIS.gov.
        These external sites have their own privacy policies, and we are not responsible for
        their content or practices. We encourage you to review the privacy policy of any external
        site you visit.
      </p>

      <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        {siteConfig.name} is intended for people preparing for the U.S. citizenship process, and
        for the family members, teachers, and community organizations who support them. It is not
        directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children
        through this website or the app.
      </p>

      <h2>Data Security</h2>
      <p>
        Study data stored locally on your device is protected by your device's own security
        features, such as a screen lock. No method of storage or transmission is completely
        secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this Privacy Policy as {siteConfig.name} grows or as our practices change.
        When we do, we will revise the "Last updated" date at the top of this page.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, you can reach us through the
        <a href={withBase('/contact')}>Contact page</a> on this website. Any information you choose
        to share when contacting us is used only to respond to you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
